<h2 id="feedback">Sending feedback</h2>
<p>
    The <strong>Feedback</strong> button in the bottom corner of every page opens a short form. Type what went
    wrong or what would help (up to 2,000 characters) and choose <strong>Send</strong>. It is filed as a help
    desk ticket in your name, so the person who picks it up can reply to you directly. You can open and close
    the form with the keyboard: <kbd>Tab</kbd> to the button, <kbd>Enter</kbd> to open, <kbd>Esc</kbd> to
    close.
</p>
<p>What is sent with your message:</p>
<ul>
    <li>the name of this app and the version that is running,</li>
    <li>the address of the page you were on, with anything that looks like a sign-in token, an email address or
        a student number removed before it leaves the app,</li>
    <li>your email address, as the person to reply to,</li>
    <li>the name of your browser.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    <strong>Screenshots.</strong> Ticking <em>Include a screenshot of this page</em> asks your browser to share
    one picture of a tab you choose. A screenshot shows everything on that screen, so if any student
    information is visible, leave the box unticked and describe the problem in words instead. The box is off
    by default, and your organization may switch it off entirely.
</p>
<p>Do not type student names or numbers into the message; the page address is enough for us to find it.</p>
